  "body": "As a customer (web surfer), I'd like to know the accuracy of the information in the web page I am looking for.\r\nwith time (new laws, technology....) an information can be obsolete.\r\nHaving the release date by default thanks a html tag, I would be more efficient to evaluate the truth of the information.\r\n possible tag \\<pagedate\\>\r\nMy thought was : \r\nI try often to check information/story accuracy  I found on social media or search engine.\r\nAnd there is something I hardly can find in a personal page or non journalist page : the date of the release .\r\nSo why not to include a tag in all html pages which will take automatically the date of the push  in the web host ?",
